# 1,10-Phenanthroline + 10 MeOH: XTB2 MD, spherical confinement
# FIXED: this file had two problems.
#   1) The MeOH block was truncated mid-copy: only 50 of the expected 60
#      solvent atoms were present (molecule No. 9 was missing its 3 methyl/
#      hydroxyl H's, and molecule No. 10 was entirely absent), so the file
#      would not even parse as a valid structure.
#   2) The placement/Cell Sphere still used Apixaban-scale parameters (offset
#      12.78 Ang, sphere radius enlarged to 18.0 but still centered on
#      Apixaban's old centroid (31.537, -19.865, -0.109)), not rescaled for
#      this much smaller solute.
#
# This version:
#   - Restores the complete 10 MeOH molecules (60 atoms), reusing the same
#     well-formed internal MeOH geometry already used for the Apixaban
#     Explicit10 MeOH work, rigidly translated (orientation preserved) to
#     new anchor points around Phenanthroline.
#   - Phenanthroline centroid for THIS geometry/orientation = (29.827,
#     -18.397, 1.407); max atom-centroid distance = 4.60 Ang.
#   - 10 MeOH molecules placed (by their own centroid) at offset 7.5 Ang from
#     Phenanthroline's centroid, along the same 12 directions used throughout
#     this project.
#   - Cell Sphere radius set to 12.0 Ang, centered on Phenanthroline's own
#     centroid (29.827, -18.397, 1.407).
# Checked: min MeOH-Phenanthroline atom distance = 2.27 Ang (no clash), max
#   atom distance from the sphere center = 8.91 Ang (safely inside the 12.0
#   Ang sphere). Total atom count = 82 (22 + 10x6), verified.

! XTB2 MD

%md
  Timestep 1.0_fs
  Initvel 298.15_K
  Thermostat NHC 298.15_K Timecon 20.0_fs
  Cell Sphere 29.827, -18.397, 1.407, 12.0 Spring 20
  Dump Position Stride 100 Filename "Phenanthroline_10MeOH_XTB.xyz"
  Run 20000
end

* xyz 0 1
